{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall lay his hand.</b> It would appear from the plain sense that he lays [hand] with one hand, for the procedure of the scapegoat is not like the procedure of every offering; therefore the verse changed and said ידו. But we find that the transmitters transmitted that every semikhah is with two hands, and we rely upon them. Also, the offering brought to make atonement for the burnt-offering — on account of the spirit it is called עולה; likewise the offering brought on account of a חטאת and an אשם is called חטאת and אשם." "<b>And it shall be accepted for him.</b> It brings favor from HaShem." "<b>To make atonement for him.</b> To be a ransom for the punishment that is upon him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved הכ׳ as הכתוב (the verse), the standard abbreviation in Ibn Ezra's commentary."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:22.864123117Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}